The information regarding Rassimov's location was given by [[Zhalia Moon]], who undercover at the [[Blood Spiral Base|Blood Spiral base]], overheard him pitch a secret mission to [[Harrison Fears]] regarding the [[Necklace of Tutankhamun]].

After [[Ariel]] erased the team's footsteps, the plan was set in motion when Rassimov was about to enter the [[Tomb of Tutankhamun]]. A coordinated sequence of attacks by the Huntik team, aided by Ariel's tornado to hinder Rassimov's vision, countered his [[magic]] while Harrison was fighting [[Den Fears]]. Rassimov then tried to use his most powerful spell, [[Darkvoid]], to get himself out of the situation. This was already expected by the Huntik team, as [[Dante Vale|Dante]] invoked [[Maelstrom]] to absorb his power. Now completely cornered, he was restrained and taken by two [[Huntik Foundation]] members in a vehicle, his [[Titans]] being taken by Dante. Harrison then ran away and used [[Powermark]] on a [[Bazela's Insect]], recovering quickly from the encounter.

However, as the team explored the tomb, Harrison attacked the vehicles taking Rassimov. Dante and company then encountered them on the way back. A fight ensues where the Huntik team have the upper hand, but things take a turn for the worse when Rassimov invokes [[Legion]], whose amulet was hidden inside his body. The team struggles heavily against the nigh-invincible Legendary Titan of War, and it manages to absorve [[Solwing]] and [[Lindorm]], with Rassimov taking the Necklace of Tutankhamun. Dante is then forced to retreat and take everyone injured to a Huntik Foundation hospital, and the mission is ultimately unsuccessful. {{Source|Rassimov's Secret}}

The mission was so exhausting for the team that even in the following days, Dante could not invoke [[Caliban]] and was overall too tired to fight or use any magic. {{Source|Back Home}}
